2186045417] [17592186520439 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ec37af3f-2077-53c3-aed3-459ba8fcb5e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520443 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520443 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520443 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520443 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520443 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520443 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520443 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520443 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186520180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520443 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fd3b5bb7-8ff5-583c-95ec-4d9a61d8d3e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520449 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520449 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146238" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520449 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520449 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,1.5)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(1+2{y}^{2})}{5}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1.5]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1.5)$ is shown above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520449 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0729c3e7-6c49-5561-ba72-ac80cc555328" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520449 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1.5] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1.5)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{3(1+2{y}^{2})}{5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520451 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520451 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146337" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520451 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520451 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(x+{y}^{2})}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x+1}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520451 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "13aa670b-3e27-50cc-b24b-f562a4443719" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520451 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3x+{y}^{2}}{8})}{(\\frac{3x+1}{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(x+{y}^{2})}{3x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{3(1+{y}^{2})}{3\\cdot 1+1}=\\frac{3(1+{y}^{2})}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{3(1+{y}^{2})}{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+{y}^{3})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4})-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520452 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520452 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146517" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520452 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520452 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6(x+y)}{5}, & x\\le y\\le 2x,\\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520452 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "200b9c27-2539-5e86-b17a-fa5314a06310" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520452 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6(x+y)}{5})}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+y)}{5{x}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\le y\\le 2x,\\,0<x<1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of 